WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.729
The first morning of the semester at a campus IT service desk, and the line is out the door.

2
00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:16.073
Lena manages the desk. Last year the surge ran the team: tickets came in late, got redone, or quietly dropped,

3
00:00:16.123 --> 00:00:22.293
and she found out on the due date. This year she runs the surge, with four habits.

4
00:00:22.343 --> 00:00:30.181
Plan it: before the doors open, three priorities on the glass wall, each with a technician’s name on it.

5
00:00:30.231 --> 00:00:38.070
Say it: each technician has a short written checklist, what they own, by when, and what good looks like,

6
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.773
on paper, not in Lena’s head. Check it: Wednesday, not Friday,

7
00:00:42.823 --> 00:00:49.676
Lena leans over a shoulder and looks at the ticket queue while there is still time to help.

8
00:00:49.726 --> 00:00:54.758
Fix it: when the same password reset comes back for the third time,

9
00:00:54.808 --> 00:01:01.130
she and a senior technician trace it to the cause at the rack, and change something,

10
00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:08.260
instead of fixing it a fourth time. By Friday the line is short and nobody worked the weekend.

11
00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:14.784
Notice what Lena stopped doing: assuming the team knew, sending the goal in one email,

12
00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:20.928
checking only when it was late, and doing the work herself because it was faster.

13
00:01:20.978 --> 00:01:26.693
This week: pick one person and confirm, out loud, what they own and by when.

